                <pb facs="0188" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2621: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commissioner in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-17T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Your telegram No. 32 of October 11, 9 a.m.</p>
                <p>Department and the Navy Department both approve the wording of the proclamation.
                    You are authorized furthermore to determine the date of the installation of the
                    Provisional Government in accord with the Military Governor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
